(2054508, 277020, 43667, '<td valign="top">This is a stained glass mosaic that I made in high school; backlit by a flashlight.  The overly bright center seems to make it more foreboding.</td>', 'This is a stained glass mosaic that I made in high school; backlit by a flashlight.  The overly bright center seems to make it more foreboding.', '2006-01-18 14:08:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054563, 276708, 32854, '<td valign="top">Nice, very very nice. It comes off the screen.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-18 14:32:55.</i></td>', 'Nice, very very nice. It comes off the screen.', '2006-01-18 14:32:38.000000', '2006-01-18 14:32:55.000000', 0),
(2054792, 276708, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8.  The colors and lighting and OOF ''circles'' really made it in my opinion.  I wondered what type of flower this is and thought it was real, but on closer inspection - perhaps it is ''fabric''(?).  If so, the fact that you ''hid'' that so well (mostly via angle/lighting/water effects) created a good illusion.  The only real ''criticism'' I may have had, and very minor, would be (again, especially for this size), to have had perhaps a little more ''height''.  If this <i>is</i> a real flower, and you know what type it is, if you could include the name in your comments, I''d be interested.  Nice shot and yes, ''Congratulations''. edit:even better then (I thought ''perhaps'' it may have been ''colored'' whilst voting, that or a flower I didn''t recognize - it was only after looking closer today I ''wondered'' whether it was fabric), thank you for including that information.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-18 15:55:01.</i></td>', 'I gave this an 8.  The colors and lighting and OOF ''circles'' really made it in my opinion.  I wondered what type of flower this is and thought it was real, but on closer inspection - perhaps it is ''fabric''(?).  If so, the fact that you ''hid'' that so well (mostly via angle/lighting/water effects) created a good illusion.  The only real ''criticism'' I may have had, and very minor, would be (again, especially for this size), to have had perhaps a little more ''height''.  If this is a real flower, and you know what type it is, if you could include the name in your comments, I''d be interested.  Nice shot and yes, ''Congratulations''. edit:even better then (I thought ''perhaps'' it may have been ''colored'' whilst voting, that or a flower I didn''t recognize - it was only after looking closer today I ''wondered'' whether it was fabric), thank you for including that information.', '2006-01-18 15:34:49.000000', '2006-01-18 15:55:01.000000', 0),
(2054828, 276708, 5112, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by macrothing:</b></div><hr/><i> I gave this an 8.  The colors and lighting and OOF ''circles'' really made it in my opinion.  I wondered what type of flower this is and thought it was real, but on closer inspection - perhaps it is ''fabric''(?).  If so, the fact that you ''hid'' that so well (mostly via angle/lighting/water effects) created a good illusion.  The only real ''criticism'' I may have had, and very minor, would be (again, especially for this size), to have had perhaps a little more ''height''.  If this <i>is</i> a real flower, and you know what type it is, if you could include the name in your comments, I''d be interested.  Nice shot and yes, ''Congratulations''. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It definitely is real.  It''s a coloured daisy (a white daisy that was coloured blue); my daughter really liked them at the store when we went to look for flowers, so I got them.<br/> <br/>BTW, we tried to get them to turn purple by adding red food colouring to the water, but it didn''t work.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-18 16:26:46.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by macrothing: I gave this an 8.  The colors and lighting and OOF ''circles'' really made it in my opinion.  I wondered what type of flower this is and thought it was real, but on closer inspection - perhaps it is ''fabric''(?).  If so, the fact that you ''hid'' that so well (mostly via angle/lighting/water effects) created a good illusion.  The only real ''criticism'' I may have had, and very minor, would be (again, especially for this size), to have had perhaps a little more ''height''.  If this is a real flower, and you know what type it is, if you could include the name in your comments, I''d be interested.  Nice shot and yes, ''Congratulations''.   It definitely is real.  It''s a coloured daisy (a white daisy that was coloured blue); my daughter really liked them at the store when we went to look for flowers, so I got them. BTW, we tried to get them to turn purple by adding red food colouring to the water, but it didn''t work.', '2006-01-18 15:42:06.000000', '2006-01-18 16:26:46.000000', 0),
(2054911, 277630, 40370, '<td valign="top">Nice finish John, you did have the best image off the crowded citrus branch.</td>', 'Nice finish John, you did have the best image off the crowded citrus branch.', '2006-01-18 15:58:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054923, 276708, 19708, '<td valign="top">WOW.<br/>Magical is the best I can come up with.<br/>Congrats on the <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/rib1.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/rib1.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/rib1.gif"/></td>', 'WOW.Magical is the best I can come up with.Congrats on the ', '2006-01-18 16:02:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054982, 277975, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6.  Liked the concept and thought the use of backlighting was good.  The ''criticism'' I had was; a variation in cropping/angle (dependent of course) to get it more symmetrical/balanced (ie; top left corner out and a fraction more space, maybe, on the right), the few ''blown'' areas and just a sharper perspective/angle to ''use the backlighting'' a bit more effectively (gain more transluscence in the fins/mouths etc), would likely have made this even better in my opinion.  After reading your comments that this was in a market, likely difficult to gain a sharper perspective/perfect ''backlighting'' and yes, the ''close up'' shows a bit more detail re the backlighting, but this entry was more ''interesting'', in my opinion.</td>', 'I gave this a 6.  Liked the concept and thought the use of backlighting was good.  The ''criticism'' I had was; a variation in cropping/angle (dependent of course) to get it more symmetrical/balanced (ie; top left corner out and a fraction more space, maybe, on the right), the few ''blown'' areas and just a sharper perspective/angle to ''use the backlighting'' a bit more effectively (gain more transluscence in the fins/mouths etc), would likely have made this even better in my opinion.  After reading your comments that this was in a market, likely difficult to gain a sharper perspective/perfect ''backlighting'' and yes, the ''close up'' shows a bit more detail re the backlighting, but this entry was more ''interesting'', in my opinion.', '2006-01-18 16:22:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2055065, 278692, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 7.  I liked the concept, colors, fading focus and thought the use of backlighting was fairly good.  The detail in the filaments/''hairs'' in the ''throat'' of the flower was what I liked best about this shot.  The ''criticism'' I had was; because the focus was on the ''throat'', that needed to be sharper (sounds like the flower &amp; camera were hand-held, so a tripod or ''fixture'' may have helped), the lighting adjusted (difficult) to illuminate more of the throat and ''hairs'' in the right places.  Overall the composition was nice but if there was more space ''below'' the focal point (throat) and possibly even more height in the frame as well (depending what you had to work with of course) would have likely made this better in my opinion.  <i>temporary note: if you know the name of this flower &amp; can include it in your comments that would be good, I will check back ''later''</i></td>', 'I gave this a 7.  I liked the concept, colors, fading focus and thought the use of backlighting was fairly good.  The detail in the filaments/''hairs'' in the ''throat'' of the flower was what I liked best about this shot.  The ''criticism'' I had was; because the focus was on the ''throat'', that needed to be sharper (sounds like the flower & camera were hand-held, so a tripod or ''fixture'' may have helped), the lighting adjusted (difficult) to illuminate more of the throat and ''hairs'' in the right places.  Overall the composition was nice but if there was more space ''below'' the focal point (throat) and possibly even more height in the frame as well (depending what you had to work with of course) would have likely made this better in my opinion.  temporary note: if you know the name of this flower & can include it in your comments that would be good, I will check back ''later''', '2006-01-18 16:39:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2055115, 279028, 40370, '<td valign="top">Wow ... this was one of my favs in the challenge, was thinking top ten, there was a lot of good competition in Backlighting. Look forward to meeting you at the GTG in Southern Utah.</td>', 'Wow ... this was one of my favs in the challenge, was thinking top ten, there was a lot of good competition in Backlighting. Look forward to meeting you at the GTG in Southern Utah.', '2006-01-18 16:53:01.000000', NULL, 0),
