(2070220, 276708, 47483, '<td valign="top">when i was doing Henri Cartier-Bresson for tribute challenge, i was thinking about two ribbons you won recently. Crisp images, wonderful photos for eyes. They are comple delight to watch. And no wonder they won ribbons. <br/>But then i was thinking about my entery for tribute challenge, solid composition, but will score near 5, since its not crisp and not an eye delight. I asked myself what do i want to do, do i want to shoot flowers with 1.4 lense and make them eye candy or do i want to take pictures like whom i am giving tribute. His pictures are not eye candy but are strong on compositions. Then i asked myself would any of his pictures would have won ribbon here. My answer is mostly ''no''. They would not have won more ribbons than you have with flowers. <br/>The thing i want to say is, your pics are wonderful but they are not great, i wish you become great photographer as i think you can do it. But then i think how many blues you want to win first.</td>', 'when i was doing Henri Cartier-Bresson for tribute challenge, i was thinking about two ribbons you won recently. Crisp images, wonderful photos for eyes. They are comple delight to watch. And no wonder they won ribbons. But then i was thinking about my entery for tribute challenge, solid composition, but will score near 5, since its not crisp and not an eye delight. I asked myself what do i want to do, do i want to shoot flowers with 1.4 lense and make them eye candy or do i want to take pictures like whom i am giving tribute. His pictures are not eye candy but are strong on compositions. Then i asked myself would any of his pictures would have won ribbon here. My answer is mostly ''no''. They would not have won more ribbons than you have with flowers. The thing i want to say is, your pics are wonderful but they are not great, i wish you become great photographer as i think you can do it. But then i think how many blues you want to win first.', '2006-01-22 08:54:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2070929, 276708, 5112, '<td valign="top">Thank you.<br/> <br/>I completely disagree that Cartier-Bresson''s photography would score low here.  I think it would do great here.  I think there is a real appreciation for his kind of photography here, but there are pathetically few images that rise to the occasion, really, really very few. <br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-22 13:37:22.</i></td>', 'Thank you. I completely disagree that Cartier-Bresson''s photography would score low here.  I think it would do great here.  I think there is a real appreciation for his kind of photography here, but there are pathetically few images that rise to the occasion, really, really very few.  ', '2006-01-22 13:24:38.000000', '2006-01-22 13:37:22.000000', 0),
