(2074264, 278680, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Greetings from Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I like it! Very nice detail.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Not as strong as it could be. Having the raspberry near dead-center isn''t exactly a strong composition. Having it off to one side of the photo would have been much stronger.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Clear, crisp .. good<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour, focus, and light):</b> <br/>Focus: Perfect. Very sharp.<br/>Colour: Also, perfect.<br/>Light: Once again, perfect.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>More than likely, a stronger composition would have gained a few points for you. Also, this was a fairly tough challenge and you scored admirably in it.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good job on this entry, you scored well with a well executed shot.<br/> <br/>Hope to see more from you soon,<br/>Leroy</td>', '::: Greetings from Critique Club :::  Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission. First Impression - the most important one: I like it! Very nice detail. Composition: Not as strong as it could be. Having the raspberry near dead-center isn''t exactly a strong composition. Having it off to one side of the photo would have been much stronger. Subject: Clear, crisp .. good Technical (Colour, focus, and light): Focus: Perfect. Very sharp.Colour: Also, perfect.Light: Once again, perfect. To grow its vote?: More than likely, a stronger composition would have gained a few points for you. Also, this was a fairly tough challenge and you scored admirably in it. Summary: Good job on this entry, you scored well with a well executed shot. Hope to see more from you soon,Leroy', '2006-01-23 12:32:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2074467, 279417, 46470, '<td valign="top">This shot should have placed much higher. Perfectly met the challenge even though it might be a bit too bright at the top right.<br/> <br/>And as usual, the model is lovely..<br/> <br/>Ones???   They''re nuts!!</td>', 'This shot should have placed much higher. Perfectly met the challenge even though it might be a bit too bright at the top right. And as usual, the model is lovely.. Ones???   They''re nuts!!', '2006-01-23 13:45:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2074954, 276878, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Greetings from Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Interesting... wild colors.. but maybe a bit more forward lighting is needed.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Centered, it''s ok. I''m not real fond of dead center compositions. I like photos that play with the rule of thirds more.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Subject is strong and definitely stands out clearly from the background.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour, focus, and light):</b> <br/>FocusL Sharp and crisp.<br/>Light: AS I stated earlier, you perhaps need more lighting from the front. What you end up with is a slightly under-exposed Santa with blown high-lights around the edges with this lighting setup.<br/>Colour: Not sure why, perhaps WB issues with multiple light sources, but the blues in the beard and coat bottom are disturbing to me.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Well, I can start b saying that DPC voters aren''t real fond of "doll" shots. So, generally they don''t score real well. <br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Was a good effort, I believe you are capable of more, especially after seeing that wonderful waterdrop shot (btw, DPC love water drops).<br/> <br/>Hope to see more from you soon,<br/>Leroy</td>', '::: Greetings from Critique Club :::  Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission. First Impression - the most important one: Interesting... wild colors.. but maybe a bit more forward lighting is needed. Composition: Centered, it''s ok. I''m not real fond of dead center compositions. I like photos that play with the rule of thirds more. Subject: Subject is strong and definitely stands out clearly from the background. Technical (Colour, focus, and light): FocusL Sharp and crisp.Light: AS I stated earlier, you perhaps need more lighting from the front. What you end up with is a slightly under-exposed Santa with blown high-lights around the edges with this lighting setup.Colour: Not sure why, perhaps WB issues with multiple light sources, but the blues in the beard and coat bottom are disturbing to me. To grow its vote?: Well, I can start b saying that DPC voters aren''t real fond of "doll" shots. So, generally they don''t score real well.  Summary: Was a good effort, I believe you are capable of more, especially after seeing that wonderful waterdrop shot (btw, DPC love water drops). Hope to see more from you soon,Leroy', '2006-01-23 16:22:24.000000', NULL, 0),
