(2078385, 278758, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC.  You now have completed your first Challenge.  Congratulations.  The first one is always the most difficult.  And I sure do like the colors you chose.<br/> <br/>You created an interesting picture here, but perhaps an unsettling one for our viewers.  Your selection of this partial mask view may have left some folks wondering what else they should be looking for.  But, of course, if you had photographed the entire mask, you might have run afoul of the "Other People''s Art" rule.  One of your commentors suggested a more symetrical view.  Now that might work, too.<br/> <br/>Your image comes across as soft.  Even with IS, sometimes it''s a good idea to brace your camera or use a tripod on these long exposures and 1/15th of a second really is a long exposure.  If you don''t want to use a tripod you might think of boosting your ISO from 50 to 100 or even 200.    <br/> <br/>All in all, I''d say this is a creditable first entry and I expect you will have a lot of fun with DPC in future challenges.  I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Welcome to DPC.  You now have completed your first Challenge.  Congratulations.  The first one is always the most difficult.  And I sure do like the colors you chose. You created an interesting picture here, but perhaps an unsettling one for our viewers.  Your selection of this partial mask view may have left some folks wondering what else they should be looking for.  But, of course, if you had photographed the entire mask, you might have run afoul of the "Other People''s Art" rule.  One of your commentors suggested a more symetrical view.  Now that might work, too. Your image comes across as soft.  Even with IS, sometimes it''s a good idea to brace your camera or use a tripod on these long exposures and 1/15th of a second really is a long exposure.  If you don''t want to use a tripod you might think of boosting your ISO from 50 to 100 or even 200.     All in all, I''d say this is a creditable first entry and I expect you will have a lot of fun with DPC in future challenges.  I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work. ', '2006-01-24 15:09:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2078570, 278775, 49007, '<td valign="top">**** Greeting from the Critique Club ****<br/> <br/>Challenge<br/>- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes<br/> <br/>Compostion<br/>- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? I like the off-centered composition, but I feel the angled horizon has a negative impact on the image. <br/>- Good use of Depth of Field? Yes The out-of-focus lighting in the background is very nice although the Bokeh of it is distracting due to the nature of your aperture blades. It would be les distracting if the lights were more circular. I''m not sure if this could be fixed with using a wider aperature or if you''d need to use a different lens.<br/>- Good focus? The focus is a bit soft on the ball, but it''s not bad.<br/> <br/>Lighting <br/>- Good use of light? Yes, but a very little soft lighting for the top of the globe work work wonders.<br/>- Good use of shadows? Yes. I love the foreground shadow and reflection on the table.<br/> <br/>Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:<br/>- Colors and Contrast Nice colors, but add a little saturation to it.<br/>- What is my reaction or feelings? Almost abstract, which I like. I don''t think voters on DPC agree with me on that opinion.</td>', '**** Greeting from the Critique Club **** Challenge- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes Compostion- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? I like the off-centered composition, but I feel the angled horizon has a negative impact on the image. - Good use of Depth of Field? Yes The out-of-focus lighting in the background is very nice although the Bokeh of it is distracting due to the nature of your aperture blades. It would be les distracting if the lights were more circular. I''m not sure if this could be fixed with using a wider aperature or if you''d need to use a different lens.- Good focus? The focus is a bit soft on the ball, but it''s not bad. Lighting - Good use of light? Yes, but a very little soft lighting for the top of the globe work work wonders.- Good use of shadows? Yes. I love the foreground shadow and reflection on the table. Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:- Colors and Contrast Nice colors, but add a little saturation to it.- What is my reaction or feelings? Almost abstract, which I like. I don''t think voters on DPC agree with me on that opinion.', '2006-01-24 15:33:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2079109, 279521, 14386, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  This looks simple in thumbnail but there is so much detail when enlarged.  Excellent composition. I like the dominant black.</td>', 'Congratulations!  This looks simple in thumbnail but there is so much detail when enlarged.  Excellent composition. I like the dominant black.', '2006-01-24 19:08:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2079387, 277589, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Very interesting idea.  I think the thought for this challenge was prefect.  The shadow was a prefect example of backlighting.  Personally I would play with the shot a little.  Like lower your angle to see a little more of the bear from the front on as opposed to the top view.  Also I think the focus could have been sharper, even though it is a dreamy bear.   If you wanted to go more with the soft focus, maybe add some more fluff possibly around the bear and still add a little more focus.  Maybe even try to focus on something like the nose so if everything else is soft there is still a focal point. <br/> <br/>Whit more detail all the little fuzzes on the bear, the shadows could have been even more striking.  I think the best part of this piece is how huge the shadow of something as small and innocent as a teddy bear is.  This idea has tons of potential in my opinion, with a little more of an angle and focus.  <br/> <br/>Good work, those first challenges are some of the hardest.  Especially putting yourself out there, so you should be proud.</td>', '*Critique Club* Very interesting idea.  I think the thought for this challenge was prefect.  The shadow was a prefect example of backlighting.  Personally I would play with the shot a little.  Like lower your angle to see a little more of the bear from the front on as opposed to the top view.  Also I think the focus could have been sharper, even though it is a dreamy bear.   If you wanted to go more with the soft focus, maybe add some more fluff possibly around the bear and still add a little more focus.  Maybe even try to focus on something like the nose so if everything else is soft there is still a focal point.  Whit more detail all the little fuzzes on the bear, the shadows could have been even more striking.  I think the best part of this piece is how huge the shadow of something as small and innocent as a teddy bear is.  This idea has tons of potential in my opinion, with a little more of an angle and focus.   Good work, those first challenges are some of the hardest.  Especially putting yourself out there, so you should be proud.', '2006-01-24 21:01:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2080036, 278460, 49007, '<td valign="top">**** Greeting from the Critique Club ****<br/> <br/>Challenge<br/>- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes, however the foreground lighting overpowers the backlighting effect. The best area to find the backlighting is in the top middle where the shaded flower contrasts nicely with the lamp light. This is how the whole image should look.<br/> <br/>Compostion<br/>- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? I like the composition the flower up front fills a good portion of the image.<br/>- Good use of Depth of Field? Yes. The light is nicely out-of-focus.<br/>- Good focus? The focus as commentor mention is a little soft. I think it works, but I''d apply a little bit of Unsharp Mask in your editor.<br/> <br/>Lighting <br/>- Good use of light? As mention before the foreground over powers the image. Less light up front for this challenge.<br/>- Good use of shadows? Yes Yes Yes. Beautiful.<br/> <br/>Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:<br/>- Colors and Contrast. The lack of color is great. You can see a little camera noise, but it works for this image.<br/>- Sharpness. Needs to be a little sharper.<br/>- What is my reaction or feelings? It''s a very strong image, and it''s too bad that others didn''t appreciate it more, but you had very heavy competetion in this challenge.<br/></td>', '**** Greeting from the Critique Club **** Challenge- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes, however the foreground lighting overpowers the backlighting effect. The best area to find the backlighting is in the top middle where the shaded flower contrasts nicely with the lamp light. This is how the whole image should look. Compostion- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? I like the composition the flower up front fills a good portion of the image.- Good use of Depth of Field? Yes. The light is nicely out-of-focus.- Good focus? The focus as commentor mention is a little soft. I think it works, but I''d apply a little bit of Unsharp Mask in your editor. Lighting - Good use of light? As mention before the foreground over powers the image. Less light up front for this challenge.- Good use of shadows? Yes Yes Yes. Beautiful. Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:- Colors and Contrast. The lack of color is great. You can see a little camera noise, but it works for this image.- Sharpness. Needs to be a little sharper.- What is my reaction or feelings? It''s a very strong image, and it''s too bad that others didn''t appreciate it more, but you had very heavy competetion in this challenge.', '2006-01-24 23:54:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2081644, 279469, 8522, '<td valign="top">Wow!</td>', 'Wow!', '2006-01-25 07:17:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2082908, 277940, 49007, '<td valign="top">Challenge<br/>- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes. Especially between the two candles.<br/>- Is subject unique (vs. unoriginal or rehashed)? Yes<br/> <br/>Compostion<br/>- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? Good composition, however I''d stand the wick up and trim it a little.<br/>- Good use of Depth of Field? Yes.<br/>- Good focus? Yes.<br/> <br/>Lighting <br/>- Good use of light? The light is on the bright side across the top of the candles. Soften it some.<br/> <br/>Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:<br/>- Colors and Contrast. I''m assuming that the candle on the right is a greenish one, but the color is lost in the reflected sun. Anyway, color isn''t important in this image. The contrast is great with the white candle against the dark background and the light through the candle contrasting with the other candle.<br/>- What is my reaction or feelings? I like this image it''s a nicely done macro.<br/></td>', 'Challenge- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes. Especially between the two candles.- Is subject unique (vs. unoriginal or rehashed)? Yes Compostion- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? Good composition, however I''d stand the wick up and trim it a little.- Good use of Depth of Field? Yes.- Good focus? Yes. Lighting - Good use of light? The light is on the bright side across the top of the candles. Soften it some. Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:- Colors and Contrast. I''m assuming that the candle on the right is a greenish one, but the color is lost in the reflected sun. Anyway, color isn''t important in this image. The contrast is great with the white candle against the dark background and the light through the candle contrasting with the other candle.- What is my reaction or feelings? I like this image it''s a nicely done macro.', '2006-01-25 13:24:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2085381, 279417, 16106, '<td valign="top">Nice technique, feathery fill lighting, wether bounced or augmented it works well. The framing is nice the rigidity and centerness of the window sets up the curves of the model. The color with the exception of the over red thigh,( incandecet bulb as fill? try using a full spectrum bulb if so, you wont get the orange tone to the light) is nicely handled.<br/> How this fared so poorly is beyond me. Had you replaced this beautiful woman with a fresh bell pepper you would have garnered many fewer votes below five, but some subjects blind certain viewers to the quality of a shot.</td>', 'Nice technique, feathery fill lighting, wether bounced or augmented it works well. The framing is nice the rigidity and centerness of the window sets up the curves of the model. The color with the exception of the over red thigh,( incandecet bulb as fill? try using a full spectrum bulb if so, you wont get the orange tone to the light) is nicely handled. How this fared so poorly is beyond me. Had you replaced this beautiful woman with a fresh bell pepper you would have garnered many fewer votes below five, but some subjects blind certain viewers to the quality of a shot.', '2006-01-25 23:14:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2085749, 276973, 49007, '<td valign="top">Challenge<br/>- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes.<br/> <br/>Compostion<br/>- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? First the background. I think there should be more velvety folds, not less. The image is nicely composed. Not quite centered, which is my style.<br/>- Good use of Depth of Field? I can''t tell if the sfotness is due to the narrow DOF or if you went crazy with NeatImage. There are parts of the image that are soft right next to parts that are details. It doesn''t quite look natural. Maybe you should have gone for a wider DOF?<br/> <br/>Lighting <br/>- Good use of light? You have good light, but you also have some blown highlights on the handle. Soft the light or under-expose it to give us more details in the feathers in the center.<br/>- Good use of shadows? Yes. The shadows are good on the front of the handles and the front of the bag has a nice gradual shading.<br/> <br/>Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:<br/>- Colors and Contrast. Good job on the contrast between the light pink and the black.<br/>- What is my reaction or feelings? Well, I gave it a 6 and you had heavy competition in backlighting. I keep leaning in to look at the feathers on the right edge. I love the details over there.</td>', 'Challenge- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes. Compostion- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? First the background. I think there should be more velvety folds, not less. The image is nicely composed. Not quite centered, which is my style.- Good use of Depth of Field? I can''t tell if the sfotness is due to the narrow DOF or if you went crazy with NeatImage. There are parts of the image that are soft right next to parts that are details. It doesn''t quite look natural. Maybe you should have gone for a wider DOF? Lighting - Good use of light? You have good light, but you also have some blown highlights on the handle. Soft the light or under-expose it to give us more details in the feathers in the center.- Good use of shadows? Yes. The shadows are good on the front of the handles and the front of the bag has a nice gradual shading. Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:- Colors and Contrast. Good job on the contrast between the light pink and the black.- What is my reaction or feelings? Well, I gave it a 6 and you had heavy competition in backlighting. I keep leaning in to look at the feathers on the right edge. I love the details over there.', '2006-01-26 00:35:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2085774, 276973, 16241, '<td valign="top">my daughter would kill for a bag like this ;)<br/></td>', 'my daughter would kill for a bag like this ;)', '2006-01-26 00:49:29.000000', NULL, 0),
